WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.592
Writing detection rules is not merely a technical exercise.

2
00:00:03.592 --> 00:00:12.592
It requires curiosity, communication, operational awareness, and empathy for analysts who rely on alerts during stressful situations.

3
00:00:12.592 --> 00:00:16.813
Effective detection engineers focus on outcomes rather than alert counts.

4
00:00:16.813 --> 00:00:26.531
They ask whether a rule helps defenders make better decisions, whether it fits the investigation workflow, and whether it gives enough context to act responsibly.

5
00:00:26.531 --> 00:00:27.958
Collaboration matters.

6
00:00:27.958 --> 00:00:39.542
Detection engineers benefit from feedback from SOC analysts, incident responders, threat hunters, IT teams, cloud teams, identity teams, and application owners.

7
00:00:39.542 --> 00:00:44.122
Each group understands part of the environment and can help improve signal quality.

8
00:00:44.122 --> 00:00:58.699
Sustainable detection engineering depends on habits: document decisions, track assumptions, test changes, review performance, retire rules that no longer add value, and improve detections as the environment changes.

9
00:00:58.699 --> 00:01:03.807
The objective is helping defenders identify and investigate activity that matters.
